{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war","id":1289594,"title":"what did the gods get out of the primordial war?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-19T11:20:00-08:00","id":1289594,"title":"what did the gods get out of the primordial war?","content":"The incarnae obviously became their own masters and got the games of divinity.. i suppose that since they sometimes let other gods play the games as well, some gods also gained some benefit<br /> <br /> But for the most part, what did the vast majority gain? the ruleship of the primordials was replaced by that of the incarnae on heaven and the exalted on earth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:26:45-08:00","id":1289596,"title":"","content":"Assuming the background is similar, the Primordials/those who created the gods geased them to be unable to revolt against them. (I do not think that this is/was limited to the Incarnae.) Thus, the gods were essentially liberated from slavery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:31:55-08:00","id":1289599,"title":"","content":"Leisure time and easier jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:34:17-08:00","id":1289600,"title":"","content":"The Unconquered Sun takes a tithe of 10% of all prayer to fund the Celestial Bureaucracy. I imagine that under Primordial rule, prayer taxes were likely more confiscatory and arbitrary, lacking the magnanimity and justice of Ignis Divine. <br /> <br /> In short, they got rich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:05:15-08:00","id":1289618,"title":"","content":"Another thing to note is that despite the rulership over the gods still being fundamentally authoritarian, there are definitely differences between the <i>flavors</i> of authority they are under. With the Primordials, you've got a basically whimsical and, in many cases, rather sadistic set of overlords who view you as a thing they created, and who find it relatively easy to replace you, should you draw their ire. With the Incarnae, you've got rulers who are the same basic type of creature you are, who presumably have at least some degree of empathy with your situation. And with the Unconquered Sun at the top, you have a ruler who's metaphysically dedicated to the principles of Temperance, Compassion, Valor, and Conviction, meaning he'll generally be careful to avoid excessive indulgence, have compassion towards you, bravely face enemies that threaten you, and hold true to his promises, all extremely useful things in a ruler. <br /> <br /> There have been plenty of rebellions in real-world history where the basic goal wasn't &quot;overthrow the ruling class and establish a democracy&quot; but rather &quot;replace our current corrupt and cruel leader with one we expect will do better for us&quot;. That the gods in Exalted actually more-or-less <i>got</i> that means it probably ranks among the more successful revolts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:16:40-08:00","id":1289624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war#post1289594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for the most part, what did the vast majority gain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being functionaries instead of slaves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war#post1289594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the ruleship of the primordials was replaced by that of the incarnae on heaven and the exalted on earth</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the gods were going from being <i>property</i> to being an <i>employee</i>. That's a big step up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289600#post1289600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun takes a tithe of 10% of all prayer to fund the Celestial Bureaucracy. I imagine that under Primordial rule, prayer taxes were likely more confiscatory and arbitrary, lacking the magnanimity and justice of Ignis Divine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The enemies of the gods <i>couldn't</i> tax the gods of their ambrosia in the Time Before, because gods <i>didn't get</i> ambrosia, because they didn't live in Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:34:27-08:00","id":1289631,"title":"","content":"Have you freaking seen the description of what it's like to live in Heaven?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:44:34-08:00","id":1289635,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war\">why</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them\">all</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi\">these</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1182319-do-the-other-yozis-stats-work-like-the-ebon-dragon-s\">threads</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157124-is-the-spiral-with-its-seven-coils-from-shards-of-the-exalted-realm-canon\">from</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1156256-why-are-the-yozis-prisons-intentionally-flawed\">you</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141085-how-long-did-the-primordial-war-lasted\">about</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1140560-why-were-the-terms-of-surrender-so-harsh-for-the-primordials\">the</a> Primordial War, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1492_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1492\" data-vbnamecard=\"1492\">mark</a>? The game takes place more than six thousand years after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-19-2019, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:55:36-08:00","id":1289641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289631#post1289631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you freaking seen the description of what it's like to live in Heaven?!</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to qualify the intended tone of this statement, as it occurs to me it might read as hostile. My meaning was more to imply a sense of awed rapture for the described glory and luxury of life in Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:00:43-08:00","id":1289645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289624#post1289624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The enemies of the gods <i>couldn't</i> tax the gods of their ambrosia in the Time Before, because gods <i>didn't get</i> ambrosia, because they didn't live in Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tax is also used to give it back as income as the incarnae have no need for ambrosia as they have unlimited access to celestial peaches and wine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:18:58-08:00","id":1289754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289635#post1289635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war\">why</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them\">all</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi\">these</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1182319-do-the-other-yozis-stats-work-like-the-ebon-dragon-s\">threads</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157124-is-the-spiral-with-its-seven-coils-from-shards-of-the-exalted-realm-canon\">from</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1156256-why-are-the-yozis-prisons-intentionally-flawed\">you</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141085-how-long-did-the-primordial-war-lasted\">about</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1140560-why-were-the-terms-of-surrender-so-harsh-for-the-primordials\">the</a> Primordial War, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1492_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1492\" data-vbnamecard=\"1492\">mark</a>? The game takes place more than six thousand years after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game takes place at whatever time in history the players' want. I like the idea of playing War in Heaven games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:41:24-08:00","id":1289780,"title":"","content":"Understanding the Primordial War can have in-play effects in any age. For example, playing Celestials whose Lytek-granted memories stretch back that far can make those times and struggles meaningful, which includes the default setting of Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:07:01-08:00","id":1289790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289600#post1289600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun takes a tithe of 10% of all prayer to fund the Celestial Bureaucracy. I imagine that under Primordial rule, prayer taxes were likely more confiscatory and arbitrary, lacking the magnanimity and justice of Ignis Divine.<br /> <br /> In short, they got rich.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is technically inaccurate in the details, but I think ultimately gets to the essential principle of the thing.<br /> <br /> The Primordials reside in Yu-Shan, luxuriating in its splendour, which would probably still be empowered primarily by the prayer of the life below.<br /> <br /> The gods reside in Creation, barred from Yu-Shan. They are bound in thankless labour, to preserve the world that offers its spiritual riches up for the Primordials to enjoy.<br /> <br /> When the gods finally get to Yu-Shan, the Unconquered Sun's tithe is actually fairly magnanimous; it disperses the riches of Heaven among the populace, disproportionate to the manner in which its natural mechanisms would do so. Your average filing clerk god will not enjoy the luxuries that Ahlat does, but by the grace of the Unconquered Sun, their labour is rewarded with regular infusions of ambrosia of their very own. They wouldn't be getting it any other way; who is going to offer their prayers to some nameless, faceless filing clerk god? But the Celestial Order ensured that even they get to enjoy at least a taste of the splendours of Heaven. What will you craft your ambrosia into? Luxuriant silken robes? A little jade and sapphire song bird to wake you each morning with pleasant tones? An ornamental fountain of rainbow fire?<br /> <br /> It's a lot more than you had living back on the slopes of Mount Meru. Praise be to the Unconquered Sun, that he did not jealously hoard all of the fruits of the victory of his Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:55:01-08:00","id":1289807,"title":"","content":"Better working and living conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T22:10:35-08:00","id":1289810,"title":"","content":"The benefits afforded to Terrestrial gods are somewhat less clear, but if I was going primarily by First Edition, I would see a big part of that as being a lot of their workload being relieved by twin factors of humanity's tenure over the Earth being somewhat less tumultuous than the activities of the likes of Dragon Kings and whatever weirder species the Primordials patronised... plus how back then, the setting had the elementals as something entirely new, created to take up a lot of the maintenance work, and how all they really needed to do was report observations about their domains, that the Celestial Bureaucracy would process back down to the level of the Realm's government, who would dispatch Terrestrial Exalted to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Maybe also a greater chance at being included in some local festivities.<br /> <br /> Some of those assumptions have changed for Third Edition, but I think the basic framework could still be salvaged. In any case, it's an answer for somebody asking primarily about Second Edition stuff, so most of the ideas transfer directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T02:07:35-08:00","id":1289851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289596#post1289596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the background is similar, the Primordials/those who created the gods geased them to be unable to revolt against them. (I do not think that this is/was limited to the Incarnae.) Thus, the gods were essentially liberated from slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>aren't superior gods capable of issuing a mandate of subordination against their lessers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T02:27:05-08:00","id":1289856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289596#post1289596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the background is similar, the Primordials/those who created the gods geased them to be unable to revolt against them. (I do not think that this is/was limited to the Incarnae.) Thus, the gods were essentially liberated from slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel obliged to mention that, given previous conversations, mark is probably working from 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T02:27:11-08:00","id":1289857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289851#post1289851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aren't superior gods capable of issuing a mandate of subordination against their lessers?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean an audit or some form of beuracratic censure, then yeah a god can level those against those lower in their branch than themselves. Of course we also can't ignore the old power of good old violence that one god can visit upon another. <br /> <br /> Not exactly the same as that bit from 2e where it was pretty explicit that the primordials could flat out force a god to only do the thing it was designed for regardless of its will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T02:35:35-08:00","id":1289858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289851#post1289851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aren't superior gods capable of issuing a mandate of subordination against their lessers?</div> </div> </div> </div>With a snap of their fingers? I didn't find a power like that even from quick read of Glories of the Most High in 2nd edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11221-turtleking","name":"Turtleking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T06:02:49-08:00","id":1289884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289635#post1289635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war\">why</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them\">all</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi\">these</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1182319-do-the-other-yozis-stats-work-like-the-ebon-dragon-s\">threads</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157124-is-the-spiral-with-its-seven-coils-from-shards-of-the-exalted-realm-canon\">from</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1156256-why-are-the-yozis-prisons-intentionally-flawed\">you</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141085-how-long-did-the-primordial-war-lasted\">about</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1140560-why-were-the-terms-of-surrender-so-harsh-for-the-primordials\">the</a> Primordial War, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1492_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1492\" data-vbnamecard=\"1492\">mark</a>? The game takes place more than six thousand years after that.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is a rule 2 violation. You know better than this.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:59:01-08:00","id":1289927,"title":"","content":"I don't have access to my Second Edition core book, so could somebody that does check the part of the Antagonists chapter concerned with spirits and remind us all of the rules for mandate of subordination?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:14:02-08:00","id":1289931,"title":"","content":"I can't find it anywhere in the Core, I think it's in one of the Rolls of Glorious Divininininity or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:16:58-08:00","id":1289932,"title":"","content":"Ah, here we go, it was in the Roll of Glorious Divinity 1.<br /> <br /> &quot;THE MANDATE OF SUBORDINATION As stated on page 295 of Exalted, each spirit may spend a temporary Willpower to give an irresistible order to spirits under its command. This effect constitutes a powerful unnatural mental influence Compulsion effect, which can conceivably be resisted (though it almost never is). Resisting spirits must pay one temporary Willpower per dot of Essence that the spirit giving the order possesses greater than their own. Spending the necessary Willpower allows a subordinate to resist all orders from a given greater spirit within that scene&quot;<br /> <br /> (Okay, I guess it was in the Core Book after all, I just missed it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:31:06-08:00","id":1289969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289932#post1289932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Okay, I guess it was in the Core Book after all, I just missed it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall it not being a dedicated thing, just listed among the things that gods can spend Willpower on.<br /> <br /> In any case, thank you. I was quite certain that they worked in the way that mark was alluding to, just wanted to have the specifics on display for the benefit of everybody else.<br /> <br /> Within those constraints, yes, it's apparent that the emancipation of the gods isn't quite as comprehensive as one might expect, to the extent that any given one is freed from the constraints of their superiors.<br /> <br /> Going by the depiction in the setting, it's more kind of... greatly loosened. Gods can still give almost indelible commands to those beneath them, but the circumstances and requirements for that would have been greatly reduced following the acquisition of Yu-Shan and institution of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Mind, a lot of that is in the past. In the Age of Sorrows, you probably get a lot of minor gods struggling under the burden of commands from superiors intended to enrich themselves, and while that might be an indictment in flaws in the system that the liberation of the gods failed to address, it's still the original system not working as intended.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:49:27-08:00","id":1289978,"title":"","content":"Many good responses here. The gods' reasons were, I think variable. I'll describe some others I find plausible:<br /> <br /> Personal loyalty will be a big one. The Unconquered Sun in particular is the general triumphant of Heaven, grin a flash, always on the march, under a sovereign that disdains to command his own legions. Many, many gods will owe him their personal loyalty - &quot;Where is your loyalty to The Monarch, Tah-na-pa?&quot; &quot;My loyalty is to the Ever-Victorious&quot;. Many will believe that he is the rightful and legitimate sovereign of Heaven (with the Mandate of errr.. Heaven).<br /> <br /> Authority loyalty is baked into the hierarchical structure of the bureaus. The Bureau of Fate in particular, would seem to be especially likely to fall in line with the Maidens, if they decreed that it must be so. The whole mission is to put into place the visions of what the Maidens decree must be so.<br /> <br /> Gods may have been won by the prospect of promotion and individual status - &quot;The first ones to fall in line with the rebellion will be rewarded with rank in the new order of the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> The prisoner gods in the Primordials' jails, languishing for horrific offences against the order of the world, would be won by a promise of amnesty and freedom in the new world.<br /> <br /> Ambition must have been important as well. We've talked about wealth, but the Unconquered Sun was likely promising a glorious age of high civilization; the gods of what would become the Bureau of Humanity would be persuaded by promises of opulent cities and rich networks of trade under the purview. It's likely the the Primordials kept much of their domains on a pretty tight leash to prevent risk and threat (barring exceptions like the Lintha, a low population of sapient beings, without much glory or magic).<br /> <br /> (I like this one as it emphasizes the gods as a knowing and intentional partner in the First Age, although a junior one to the genius of the Solar Exalted).<br /> <br /> War gods would be motivated by the chance for glorious struggle alone. The Aerial Legion perhaps by the chance to test their mettle against their creators.<br /> <br /> Beyond all these considerations, consider survival instincts alone on the part of the gods who would be neutral. &quot;What do you think they'll do to us, if the Incarna lose? Do you think they'll trust us again? Do you think they'll let us exist? If the Incarna win, do you think *they'll* let us live?&quot;. Once enough gods are on side that conflict becomes inevitable, they had to pick a side. The whole thing is much like a coup; you win the heads of the army who command loyalty of the others, and then you make it clear that anyone else who doesn't falls into line is for the chop.<br /> <br /> Remember finally that by the Second Age we have a sampling of the gods who won out the end of the war and the First Age successfully. This may not be a sample to represent the gods as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:43:23-08:00","id":1290037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289754#post1289754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game takes place at whatever time in history the players' want. I like the idea of playing War in Heaven games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and there is literally nothing wrong with him making a thread like this. There should be no shame in it. It\u2019s a valid point of discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:53:20-08:00","id":1290042,"title":"","content":"Also remember that the Primordials would come to Creation while taking a break from the Games (it wasn't their turn), and just mess around with Creation for fun. Or maybe to break something that another Primordial liked, just because.<br /> And the gods of those things? Instant unemployment, if the Primordial didn't decide to also mess with you.<br /> The gods got an order that wouldn't be shaken up on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T20:31:41-08:00","id":1290226,"title":"","content":"Agency. The Gods got agency over their own lives.<br /> <br /> That's a big fuckin' deal. Especially when you remember how ALIEN the Titans are. It's not just that you lack agency over your own life, but that agency resides in beings you can barely comprehend and who you suspect barely comprehend YOU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T05:36:49-08:00","id":1292121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289857#post1289857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you mean an audit or some form of beuracratic censure, then yeah a god can level those against those lower in their branch than themselves. Of course we also can't ignore the old power of good old violence that one god can visit upon another.<br /> <br /> Not exactly the same as that bit from 2e where it was pretty explicit that the primordials could flat out force a god to only do the thing it was designed for regardless of its will.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, i mean that at least in second edition the higher gods could give magic orders to inferior gods i believe. Though i could be remembering wrong<br /> <br /> By the way did the third edition explicitly say that the primordials couldn't order the gods? if not isn't it better t assume that the old canon still applies until explicitly refuted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T06:38:40-08:00","id":1292137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292121#post1292121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if not isn't it better t assume that the old canon still applies until explicitly refuted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why pick the assumption that makes the least sense, and is most problematic for the setting, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T09:33:54-08:00","id":1292189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292121#post1292121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though i could be remembering wrong</div> </div> </div> </div>No no, they were the ones who were wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way did the third edition explicitly say that the primordials couldn't order the gods? if not isn't it better t assume that the old canon still applies until explicitly refuted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not directly, but the description of Exaltation is contrary to the attitude that Second Edition took to the subject, as the basis for imagining the geas in that manner in the first place. Besides that, developers have consistently presented an attitude that it's not really how it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T09:44:56-08:00","id":1292196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292189#post1292189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not directly, but the description of Exaltation is contrary to the attitude that Second Edition took to the subject, as the basis for imagining the geas in that manner in the first place. Besides that, developers have consistently presented an attitude that it's not really how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Primordial War wouldn't have gone so well if the Yozis-to-be could have just told Luna, &quot;Okay, the second you imbue someone with your divine fire, <i>pull their heart out from their chest.</i> Better yet, just don't Exalt people.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:36:05-08:00","id":1292211,"title":"","content":"In addition to the other reasons for getting rid of the Mandate of Submission that others have mentioned (basically, it's not a good idea), I would say that <i>in general</i>, it's a bad idea to assume that 2e canon holds for 3e unless contradicted. 3e is its own thing. It should be a complete game on its own. A player or Storyteller who picks up the Exalted books starting in 3e should not have to be aware of stuff that was revealed only in a 2e or 1e book to make sense of things. For purposes of 3e canon, 2e and earlier editions basically don't exist, and I think that, if something stated as happening in 3e's history or general discussion of metaphysics doesn't make sense in terms of something stated in earlier editions, then the only reasonable assumption is that the earlier edition stuff doesn't apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:59:27-08:00","id":1292220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1289932#post1289932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, here we go, it was in the Roll of Glorious Divinity 1.<br /> <br /> &quot;THE MANDATE OF SUBORDINATION As stated on page 295 of Exalted, each spirit may spend a temporary Willpower to give an irresistible order to spirits under its command. This effect constitutes a powerful unnatural mental influence Compulsion effect, which can conceivably be resisted (though it almost never is). Resisting spirits must pay one temporary Willpower per dot of Essence that the spirit giving the order possesses greater than their own. Spending the necessary Willpower allows a subordinate to resist all orders from a given greater spirit within that scene&quot;<br /> <br /> (Okay, I guess it was in the Core Book after all, I just missed it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This will not carry over into Third Edition. We want divine politics to be driven primarily by the same issues and processes that drive real-world political interaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T11:31:49-08:00","id":1292227,"title":"","content":"... Have we established in 3E that the primordials were tyrants? They're first referred to as god monsters, but their rule was only ever referenced in a general way.<br /> <br /> Since not all gods are jerks, it may be possible a lot of them were just sick of tired of doing what the sociopathic devil-gods wanted. A lot of races probably had it pretty rough under the primordials, and there are clear examples of gods who actually care about mortals.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I would consider not having to enact the insane policies of sentient-sapient natural disasters on beings who most likely did absolutely nothing to deserve what they were going through to be a big step up in life.<br /> <br /> Edit: Granted, the new Heaven and the Exalted are by no means innocent, but it could be worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 02-26-2019, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T02:04:31-08:00","id":1292409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292196#post1292196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Primordial War wouldn't have gone so well if the Yozis-to-be could have just told Luna, &quot;Okay, the second you imbue someone with your divine fire, <i>pull their heart out from their chest.</i> Better yet, just don't Exalt people.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>my personal interpretation of the primordials being capable of ordering gods is that they could only give general orders but without being able to give specifics or close loopholes<br /> Similar to the Sun's power to order the defeated Yozis. So an order of &quot;attack your own exalted&quot; might have not gone very well if it also allowed the incarna to attack the primordials as well<br /> If you take away the primordials power to order gods then you are left with no explanation about why exaltation works the way it does. Why didn't the incarna make it so that they can choose to exalt anyone at all. Or for that matter stop the process of exaltation etc, or make it so that a newly exalted person becomes their slave immediately.etc, like an akuma with an urge/motivation to&quot; serve the will of the sun/luna/jupiter/etc<br /> <br /> Giving the pre-defeat primordials at least some minimal metaphysical authority over the gods solves these issues","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T02:20:21-08:00","id":1292415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292409#post1292409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you take away the primordials power to order gods then you are left with no explanation about why exaltation works the way it does. Why didn't the incarna make it so that they can choose to exalt anyone at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes that the gods <i>could</i> choose the way Exaltation works. In 3e, I don't think it was a designed process. The Sun didn't sit down with Autochthon and say &quot;okay, I want the Exaltations to Choose people based on these criteria, and I need an extra helping of indestructibility&quot;. The Incarnae produced the only Exaltations they <i>could </i>have produced, given their natures. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:37:49-08:00","id":1292428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292409#post1292409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you take away the primordials power to order gods then you are left with no explanation about why exaltation works the way it does. Why didn't the incarna make it so that they can choose to exalt anyone at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same reason why people like Solars and Lunars can't just make their powers work however they want, especially when it comes to things referencing their own Intimacies.<br /> <br /> Also, what do those things you're saying have to do with each other?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or for that matter stop the process of exaltation</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of their respective personalities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">etc, or make it so that a newly exalted person becomes their slave immediately.etc, like an akuma with an urge/motivation to&amp;quot; serve the will of the sun/luna/jupiter/etc</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a notion that for the Sun, something like that (and dirty bomb Exigence) was his first idea. Then he actually saw people, and found that he much preferred champions; he might be a bit too much of an idealist for his own good.<br /> <br /> Mindless slaves are a bit contrary to Luna's nature anyway, and the Maidens prefer more subtle methods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving the pre-defeat primordials at least some minimal metaphysical authority over the gods solves these issues</div> </div> </div> </div>How?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:34:22-08:00","id":1292497,"title":"","content":"I remember that the geas said the Gods couldn't <i>attack</i> the Primordials, hence needing the Exaltations. (Though I remember something about how the bravest gods attacked them indirectly, like attacking a mountain to cause a landslide which then hit some devas.) But did the geas actually make them follow orders, or was that just, you know, terror of their evil bosses?<br /> <br /> Where in 3rd ed, or 2nd ed for that matter, does it say the geas forced the Gods to obey all orders? I kind of have a feeling that's just fanon.<br /> <br /> Though considering the inconsistency of 2nd ed, it might have said &quot;the geas stopped them attacking their masters&quot; in some places, and &quot;the geas made them follow orders&quot; in others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:50:51-08:00","id":1292504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292497#post1292497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that the geas said the Gods couldn't <i>attack</i> the Primordials, hence needing the Exaltations. (Though I remember something about how the bravest gods attacked them indirectly, like attacking a mountain to cause a landslide which then hit some devas.) But did the geas actually make them follow orders, or was that just, you know, terror of their evil bosses?<br /> <br /> Where in 3rd ed, or 2nd ed for that matter, does it say the geas forced the Gods to obey all orders? I kind of have a feeling that's just fanon.<br /> <br /> Though considering the inconsistency of 2nd ed, it might have said &quot;the geas stopped them attacking their masters&quot; in some places, and &quot;the geas made them follow orders&quot; in others.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 3e, the geas specifically and solely forbade the gods (and any other beings who were of significant power at the time) from attacking the enemies of the gods. This hearkens back to its real-world mythological source, the role of mistletoe in the death of Baldr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T09:51:09-08:00","id":1292516,"title":"","content":"Speaking of real-world politics... I think it's fair to say that most lower-ranked Terrestrial deities got very little personally from the Primordial War. The reality is that it was pretty unlikely for Adrian or SWLiHN to pay them enough attention to cause problems for them; and overall their day-to-day job probably didn't change much. (While the books have described the gods as slaves, which is <i>technically</i> true, let's be real - even the lowest Terrestrial deity has always been in a position of privilege and power compared to mortals. And &quot;freedom&quot;, for many of them, meant doing the same jobs, but for the Incarnae and other deities rather than the Primordials.)<br /> <br /> <i>But</i>. You shouldn't underestimate what it means to them to notionally have the gods in charge of heaven rather than the Primordials. The post-Primordial War world is ruled by the gods (even if the Exalted rule earth, they were <i>given</i> this rulership as a mandate from the Unconquered Sun as king of heaven.) I would imagine that for the vast majority of Terrestrial deities, this alone is enough reason to see the Primordial War as a good thing.<br /> <br /> If you look at, like, real-world wars and revolutions, it's pretty similar? Most people aren't going to see drastic changes to their own lives as a result of replacing the people at the top. But things like race and culture and tribal affiliation can still make them <i>perceive</i> a huge benefit to ensuring that the person ultimately in charge is similar to them.<br /> <br /> Also, in the abstract, the actions taken by the god-ruled Heaven are probably, on the whole, slightly more to the liking of Terrestrial gods. Even if it doesn't affect them directly, your typical Terrestrial god has a lot more in common with the powerful gods of Yu-Shan or the top Terrestrial than they did with the Primordials, so when higher-up deities send down a law or proclamation, it's more likely to be something the lower deities agree with.<br /> <br /> And while there's tension between the gods and the Exalted at times, they probably, similarly, feel closer to the Exalted (who are mostly god-powered and often worship or worshipped deities) than they did to, say, the Lintha or to the various lower devas who occupied a similar role before. Their relationship with the people they work with immediately is / was probably a bit more respectful than it was under the Primordials because of this.<br /> <br /> (The Immaculate Faith obviously strains this to an extent - when the Solars died and the DBs lost the tight grip of the remnants of the Realm following the Contagion and the Fair Folk invasion, a lot of gods saw this as a chance to take even more power and freedom; and the Sidereals and DBs solved this by using a lot more physical force and much tighter constraints than the gods had been used to in the First Age. So I'd expect that there's a lot more divine grumbling in the Age of Sorrows than there was previously. But most of it is going to be either &quot;let's grab even more stuff for ourselves&quot; or somewhat idealized &quot;things were better in the First Age&quot; things, probably with the latter remembering the First Age as an era with more freedom for low ranking Terrestrial deities than they actually had - I don't think there are many gods who would want to go back to the pre-Primordial War era.)<br /> <br /> I also suspect that the UCS still has a lot more cachet among lower Terrestrial deities than the fandom often assumes; we tend to overemphasize his addiction to the games and see him through the lens of what we think he <i>could</i> be doing. To most lower Terrestrial deities, that doesn't matter - they weren't going to see the UCS up close anyway. He means a lot more to them as a symbol of &quot;gods are in charge now&quot; than any practical achievements they require from him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T09:56:04-08:00","id":1292522,"title":"","content":"Plus, he's only a reclusive depressed addict for the last 1500 years; many gods probably remember him as the hero who led them to freedom, then ruled as a righteous and just king for 5000 years.<br /> He's a once-great leader who's been doing not so great lately, but... he was still a great leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T10:54:59-08:00","id":1292531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292497#post1292497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where in 3rd ed, or 2nd ed for that matter, does it say the geas forced the Gods to obey all orders? I kind of have a feeling that's just fanon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the Second Edition corebook, somewhere near the start... check around the sidebar describing general details for the Exalted. Just across from the page with art depicting the Scarlet Empress on her throne.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:05:16-08:00","id":1292537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292531#post1292531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the Second Edition corebook, somewhere near the start... check around the sidebar describing general details for the Exalted. Just across from the page with art depicting the Scarlet Empress on her throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T12:23:55-08:00","id":1292826,"title":"","content":"Also, belatedly, something else that occurred to me: The arbitrary nature of the Primordials probably created a lot of extra work that pissed off the Terrestrial gods. Every time Kimbery decides to make it rain acid someplace, who do you think has to handle all the paperwork and repairs and effects downstream? And while the gods themselves probably wouldn't suffer from this directly the way mortals did, many of them probably had at least <i>some</i> connection to the mortals and animals in their area, so they'd be pissed at the unnecessary suffering - the Unconquered Sun rebelled in part for this reason, say.<br /> <br /> The Weather Gods are probably still seen as jerks upstairs by a lot of Terrestrial deities (the way people might see the federal government in the real world), but on the whole their plans for the weather tend to be more rational and predictable in ways that probably make it easier for Terrestrials to manage. They might send the occasional unwanted hurricane, but they're not going to make it rain acid or fire. Also, the fact that the entire system is gods now means even low-ranking Terrestrial gods have a bit more say and influence - if the Weather gods send an annoying hurricane without enough warning and it causes problems for all the terrestrial deities in an area, they're going to at least <i>hear</i> the grumbling on some level as it goes up the chain, whereas if Kimbery decided to make it rain acid you're pretty much SOL.<br /> <br /> The system is probably a lot more defunct in that respect today than it was in the First Age, but even now, I doubt there are many deities that would want to swap their annoying weather gods for Kimbery or anything like that (and that's partially based on actual annoyance / suffering / extra work the capricious nature caused them, rather than just the tribalism I outlined above.) In fact, many Terrestrial gods are probably just fine with the current defunct state, since it means even less work for them - they can get away with doing the bare minimum, and while heaven is corrupt and dysfunctional, it's dysfunctional in a way that means that it's unlikely to do <i>anything</i>, which, from the perspective of most Terrestrial deities, is just fine.<br /> <br /> Of course that changes when they face a catastrophe that requires outside help and they find Heaven isn't there for them. But the day-to-day life of your typical Terrestrial deity probably improved after the Primordial War due to those things, and (if they survived the Fair Folk Invasion + Contagion) they may even like the situation in the Age of Sorrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T11:16:31-08:00","id":1293096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1292504#post1292504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3e, the geas specifically and solely forbade the gods (and any other beings who were of significant power at the time) from attacking the enemies of the gods. This hearkens back to its real-world mythological source, the role of mistletoe in the death of Baldr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Further reading for the curious:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://norse-mythology.org/tales/the-death-of-baldur/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://norse-mythology.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/The-Death-of-Baldr-300x243.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://norse-mythology.org/tales/the-death-of-baldur/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Death of Baldur - Norse Mythology for Smart People </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://norse-mythology.org/tales/the-death-of-baldur/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://norse-mythology.org/tales/the-death-of-baldur/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Baldur was one of the most beloved of all the gods. The son of Odin, the chief of the gods, and the benevolent sorceress goddess Frigg, Baldur was a generous, joyful, and courageous character who gladdened the hearts of all who spent time with him. When, therefore, he began to have ominous dreams of some &hellip; Continue reading The Death of Baldur &rarr; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The wily and disloyal Loki</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> sensed an opportunity for mischief.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In disguise, he went to Frigg and asked her, \u201cDid <i>all</i> things swear oaths to spare Baldur from harm?\u201d \u201cOh, yes,\u201d the goddess replied, \u201ceverything except the mistletoe. But the mistletoe is so small and innocent a thing that I felt it superfluous to ask it for an oath. What harm could it do to my son?\u201d</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T11:53:55-08:00","id":1293328,"title":"","content":"You know I never thought about it until now, but shouldn't she have made <i>Loki</i> swear not to harm Baldur? That would have been a much higher priority than mistletoe and could have avoided the whole problem!<br /> <br /> Maybe he did and just ate the botches. I don't think &quot;it was the mistletoe that hurt him, not me!&quot; would fly at most tables, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T12:18:29-08:00","id":1293333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1293328#post1293328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I never thought about it until now, but shouldn't she have made <i>Loki</i> swear not to harm Baldur? That would have been a much higher priority than mistletoe and could have avoided the whole problem!<br /> <br /> Maybe he did and just ate the botches. I don't think &quot;it was the mistletoe that hurt him, not me!&quot; would fly at most tables, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>May be me, but I think Loki got around the oath by not doing it himself, tricking Hodr into doing it instead (moreover, with Hodr unaware of what would happen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 03-02-2019, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T12:45:11-08:00","id":1293337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289594-what-did-the-gods-get-out-of-the-primordial-war?p=1293328#post1293328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I never thought about it until now, but shouldn't she have made <i>Loki</i> swear not to harm Baldur? That would have been a much higher priority than mistletoe and could have avoided the whole problem!<br /> <br /> Maybe he did and just ate the botches. I don't think &amp;quot;it was the mistletoe that hurt him, not me!&amp;quot; would fly at most tables, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This in a discussion where we're talking about the fact that the gods get around the head by getting humans to harm them.<br /> <br /> I think when you've elicited an oath that outright prevents almost every being or material from inflicting direct bodily harm, closing loopholes from dissembling can feel reasonably unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I think getting the blind god to do it was a combination of plausible deniability and being a dick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T18:00:19-08:00","id":1293388,"title":"","content":"To be fair the iteration I heard on the whole Loki kills Baldr story always made it a point that since nothing was allowed to harm Baldr throwing crap at him was a game for most of the pantheon. Essentially the Aesir would throw whatever random crap they wanted at Baldr and the objects would stop or veer off randomly to avoid harming Baldr, So choosing Hodr would might have been an insulating precaution in case any promises he may or may not have sworn came into play by knowing about the mistletoe and the deniability that Loki wasn't the one who did it since it probably wouldn't have been the first time someone had taken a shot with a bow at Baldr.* Plus the old mixed deniability thing where pretty much everyone knows who's responsible, but no one can prove it satisfactorily enough to do anything about it. (See Sidereal Usurpation 2e at least.)<br /> <br /> <br /> *Honestly it was never said in an iteration, I just always assumed that when it said Frigg got everything to promise not to hurt her boy that it would have started with getting the other Aesir in out. The game being born out of a loophole that attacking Baldr was fair game so long as they didn't hurt him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-02-2019, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}